Capability → the same incision history must predict chemical inventory and directional fracture load to90days, and new load/O2/design trajectories from a sufficient local state.
Conflict → HP increases while collagen amount barely decreases; early chemistry is fast but strength recovery slow; different glycosylation branches share neither yield nor time scale.
Obstacle → absolute native precursor/glyco pool and local connected bridge state are missing; two external assay endpoints do not identify the first- versus second-order law. Normal skin day0 is no observed initial wound state.
Changed operation → measure the same skin cohort’s stoichiometric precursor→HP/other-product flux under LOX blockade and load variation, and feed these rates and connected-fibre history into a joint chemistry/mechanics checkpoint.

